    <string name="mail_hint_gmail">Gmail only allows an app password in other mail apps: switch on 2-Step Verification in your Google account, then create an app password (16 letters) and enter it here.</string>
    <string name="mail_hint_gmx">Switch on “POP3/IMAP access” once in the web mailer: Settings → POP3/IMAP. Then sign in here with your normal password.</string>
    <string name="mail_hint_tonline">T-Online needs a separate “password for e-mail programs”: create it in the T-Online e-mail center under Settings → Password, then enter it here.</string>
    <string name="mail_hint_outlook">Note: Microsoft no longer allows signing in with a password in other mail apps for Outlook.com and Hotmail (only with Microsoft\'s own sign-in, which Nova Mail does not have). Work and school accounts with an app password may still work.</string>
    <string name="mail_hint_yahoo">Yahoo and AOL only allow an app password in other mail apps: create it in your account security settings, then enter it here.</string>
    <string name="mail_hint_icloud">iCloud Mail needs an app-specific password: create it in your Apple account under Sign-In and Security, then enter it here.</string>
